@startuml
' Sources: ZIP pom.xml, application.properties, application-dev.properties,
' package/controller/repository analysis; SIDIS assignment, PL2, PL3;
' output/arq_corrigida.puml.
' Existing code: one Maven project and one Spring Boot application, not four
' separately deployed services. Packages Aircraft/AircraftCatalog -> Aircraft;
' Airport -> Airport; Route/Flight -> Route; Maintenance -> Maintenance.
' The ZIP contains no Dockerfile/Compose configuration or inter-service client.
' H2 per replica is an initial proposal using the existing database technology.
' Hosts, eight future ports, peer URLs, separate builds and replica profiles TBD.
title AISafe - Deployment and Replication\nProposed decomposition of the PSOFT monolith
left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor white

node "Route / Flight Operations" as Route {
  node "Replica A\nPort: TBD" as RA
  node "Replica B\nPort: TBD" as RB
  database "H2 local store A\nIndependent JVM" as RDA
  database "H2 local store B\nIndependent JVM" as RDB
  RA <--> RB : Peer HTTP GET
  RA --> RDA : JPA
  RB --> RDB : JPA
}
node "Aircraft Management" as Aircraft {
  node "Replica A\nPort: TBD" as AA
  node "Replica B\nPort: TBD" as AB
  database "H2 local store A\nIndependent JVM" as ADA
  database "H2 local store B\nIndependent JVM" as ADB
  AA <--> AB : Peer HTTP GET
  AA --> ADA : JPA
  AB --> ADB : JPA
}
node "Airport Management" as Airport {
  node "Replica A\nPort: TBD" as PA
  node "Replica B\nPort: TBD" as PB
  database "H2 local store A\nIndependent JVM" as PDA
  database "H2 local store B\nIndependent JVM" as PDB
  PA <--> PB : Peer HTTP GET
  PA --> PDA : JPA
  PB --> PDB : JPA
}
node "Maintenance Management" as Maintenance {
  node "Replica A\nPort: TBD" as MA
  node "Replica B\nPort: TBD" as MB
  database "H2 local store A\nIndependent JVM" as MDA
  database "H2 local store B\nIndependent JVM" as MDB
  MA <--> MB : Peer HTTP GET
  MA --> MDA : JPA
  MB --> MDB : JPA
}

Route --> Aircraft : HTTP/REST\nAircraft checks / metrics
Route --> Airport : HTTP/REST\nAirport checks
Route --> Maintenance : HTTP/REST\nMaintenance checks
Maintenance --> Aircraft : HTTP/REST\nAircraft lookup
Aircraft ..> Route : HTTP/REST\nQueries / statistics
Airport ..> Route : HTTP/REST\nQueries / statistics

legend bottom left
  Verified PSOFT baseline:
  Java 17; Spring Boot 3.3.5; Spring Web, Data JPA and Security; Maven.
  One project/application; current monolith port: 8081.
  H2 in memory: jdbc:h2:mem:testdb; default profile: dev.
  application-dev.properties uses ddl-auto=create; no Docker configuration.

  Proposed deployment:
  Each replica is a separate Spring Boot process with its own H2 store.
  All eight service ports, host placement and replica profiles: TBD.
  Use distinct ports when replicas share a host; no shared database.
  Service-level arrows summarise calls between the respective replicas.
  Peer arrows apply only within the same service; forwarding is not write sync.
  Write synchronisation, conflict handling and data redundancy: TBD.
  Inter-service authentication, TLS, access control and audit are required;
  their distributed configuration remains TBD. No message queues.
endlegend
@enduml
